section: kubernetes
title: Kubernetes version and engine
about: |
  The Kubernetes version, the release channel, and what each engine does with a change of the
  version or of the pack values.
rules:
- id: skip-k8s-upgrade
  title: No pool skips the Kubernetes upgrade
  engines:
  - all
  tier: static
  severity: note
  status: source
  what: |
    A pool with `skipK8sUpgrade: enabled` keeps its Kubernetes version when the cluster
    upgrades. The `repave` level of strata says the whole cluster rolls; for that pool it does
    not. The scope is each machine pool of the entity, on every engine.
  check:
    kind: static
    expr: |
      [ .entity.spec.machinepoolconfig[]
        | select((.poolConfig.skipK8sUpgrade // "") as $s | $s == "enabled" or $s == true)
        | "pool \(.poolConfig.name) sets skipK8sUpgrade \(.poolConfig.skipK8sUpgrade): a Kubernetes bump does not roll this pool, so the repave level of strata does not hold for it" ]
  evidence:
  - kind: run
    ref: '#73'
  - kind: source
    note: an enum of enabled and disabled on each pool config
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/eks/skip-upgrade.json
    clean: fixtures/eks/clean.json
- id: gke-repave-answers
  title: The change of the GKE cluster repaves no node pool
  engines:
  - gke
  tier: palette
  severity: warn
  status: seen
  when: .clusterUid != null and .before != null
  what: |
    On GKE, a bump of the `kubernetes-gke` tag repaves. The four GKE packs (`cos-gke`,
    `kubernetes-gke`, `cni-vpc-native-gke`, `gke-csi-gcp-driver`) have values of comments alone,
    so an edit of their values changes no root of strata and repaves nothing. `validate/repave`
    gives the answer before the change is applied. This rule warns when Palette says the change
    repaves, and when the Kubernetes tag changes and Palette says it does not, which contradicts
    run #90.
  check:
    kind: palette
    method: POST
    path: /v1/spectroclusters/{{ .clusterUid }}/validate/repave
    body: '{profiles: .entity.spec.profiles}'
    saves: console-address
    expr: |
      def k8s_tag(e): [ e | (.spec.profiles // [])[] | (.packValues // [])[] | select((.name // "") | test("^kubernetes")) | .tag ] | .[0];
      def reasons: [ (.response.body.reasons // [])[] | "\(.code // "?"): \(.message // "") [\(.pack.target.name // .pack.current.name // "?")]" ] | join("; ");
      if (.response.ok | not) then ["Palette refused validate/repave: \(.response.body.code // .response.status): \(.response.body.message // "")"]
      else
        (.response.body.isRepaveRequired // false) as $r
        | k8s_tag(.before) as $b | k8s_tag(.entity) as $a
        | [ if $r then "Palette repaves the GKE cluster for this change; GKE rolls each node pool: \(reasons)" else empty end ]
          + [ if ($b != null and $a != null and $b != $a and ($r | not))
              then "the kubernetes-gke tag changes \($b) to \($a), and Palette says no repave; run #90 saw a repave for a Kubernetes bump"
              else empty end ]
      end
  reproduce:
  - '{{ palette_curl }} -X POST -H ''Content-Type: application/json'' "${PALETTE_API:-https://api.spectrocloud.com}/v1/spectroclusters/{{ .clusterUid }}/validate/repave" -d @<(jq ''{profiles: .spec.profiles}'' entity.json) | jq ''{isRepaveRequired, reasons: [.reasons[] | {code, message}]}''{{ saves_comment("console-address") }}'
  evidence:
  - kind: run
    ref: '#90'
    note: a Kubernetes bump repaved; the values of the four GKE packs are comments alone
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/gke/repave-k8s-bump.json
    clean: fixtures/gke/repave-none.json
